DESCRIPTION:National Hugging Day falls on January 21 and is one of the rare
  modern observances whose founder is both known and still running it. Kevi
 n Zaborney created it in 1986 in Caro\, Michigan\, and placed it deliberat
 ely in late January\, when the holidays are over and winter is not. Four d
 ecades on\, its organizers spend as much effort on consent\, and on altern
 atives for people who do not want to be touched\, as on hugging itself.\n\
